  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\n{備|び} (prepare, equip) + {蓄|ちく} (store, accumulate)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {食料|しょくりょう}{備蓄|びちく} - food stockpile\n- {石油|せきゆ}{備蓄|びちく} - oil reserves\n- {備蓄|びちく}{品|ひん} - stockpiled goods\n- {備蓄|びちく}{倉庫|そうこ} - stockpile warehouse\n- {緊急|きんきゅう}{備蓄|びちく} - emergency reserves\n\nDISASTER PREPAREDNESS:\nIn Japan, households are encouraged to stockpile:\n- {水|みず} - water (3 liters per person per day)\n- {非常食|ひじょうしょく} - emergency food\n- {懐中電灯|かいちゅうでんとう} - flashlight\n- {乾電池|かんでんち} - batteries\n- {救急|きゅうきゅう}セット - first aid kit\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {貯蔵|ちょぞう} - storage, preservation\n- {蓄|たくわ}え - reserves, savings\n- {物資|ぶっし} - supplies, goods",
